  "details": "- Rebase to gimp-3.0.4-4.el9_8.15\n- CVE-2026-106062: take the vendor's DDS loader patch in place of ours and keep\n  the two upstream fixes it lacks: a checked linear buffer size and layer\n  allocation on 32-bit, and a buffer overrun on uncompressed rows\n- CVE-2026-112257: reject a PSD JPEG thumbnail that is not RGB (vendor patch)\n- CVE-2026-112258: remove freed XCF layers and channels from the linked lists,\n  including the selection channel, which the vendor's patch misses\n- CVE-2026-112261: drop a duplicate or failed path from the XCF selected path\n  list (vendor patch)\n- Replace our PCX loader bytes-per-line hardening with the upstream fix, which\n  widens the value to gsize instead of rejecting a 65536-pixel-wide image",
